sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Unlike rule-based systems, which can be run directly, systems defined by constraints offer no direct procedure for finding the patterns they allow; one must search from outside the system, which can take enormous computational effort.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Constraint systems require going outside the system to find their patterns";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Systems Based on Constraints” (from p. 210), p. 217. Scope: systems defined by constraints versus explicit evolution rules"
}
